      "lang": "en",
      "note_tweet": {
        "text": "The fascinating part is that the same DNA can be read differently by different cells. A single-letter change might disrupt an enhancer that is active in immune cells but largely inactive in the heart or brain.\n\nThe real promise of AlphaGenome 2 is connecting genetic variants to the specific cells where disease begins. The next challenge is validating those predictions experimentally. 🧬"
      },
