                "expanded_url": "http://alphagenome.google",
                "start": 136,
                "url": "https://t.co/JuHxlKRSci"
              }
            ]
          },
          "text": "Not fully open-source: client code is Apache-licensed, but AlphaGenome 2 runs via free API for non-commercial research only (get key at https://t.co/JuHxlKRSci). Commercial is private preview (no public pricing yet).\n\nReal uses: research on disease drivers—e.g., how variants hit specific cells in IBD, immune responses, diabetes or heart conditions—to prioritize experiments and GWAS hits. Research-only, not clinical.\n\nLayman workflows: none practical. Needs DNA sequences, cell data, Python/API skills. Scientists use Colab tutorials to score variants under cell conditions. Not for personal genetics."
        },
